{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LAdBjAxbxKX4r1GeHdnSTh","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→{\n     2→  \"metadata\": {\n     3→    \"title\": \"Masque of the Red Death - Poe\",\n     4→    \"author\": \"Edgar Allan Poe\",\n     5→    \"source_file\": \"Test_Texts/Masque of the Red Death - Poe.txt\",\n     6→    \"source_format\": \"txt\",\n     7→    \"total_word_count\": 2449,\n     8→    \"total_character_count\": 13811,\n     9→    \"estimated_total_duration_minutes\": 16.286666666666665,\n    10→    \"words_per_minute\": 150\n    11→  },\n    12→  \"structure\": [\n    13→    {\n    14→      \"type\": \"chapter\",\n    15→      \"title\": null,\n    16→      \"index\": 1,\n    17→      \"start_position\": 28,\n    18→      \"end_position\": 13811,\n    19→      \"word_count\": 2443,\n    20→      \"estimated_duration_minutes\": 16.286666666666665,\n    21→      \"confidence\": \"medium\",\n    22→      \"children\": [],\n    23→      \"characters_present\": [\n    24→        \"Prince Prospero\",\n    25→        \"The masked figure (Red Death)\",\n    26→        \"Courtiers\",\n    27→        \"Musicians\",\n    28→        \"Buffoons\",\n    29→        \"Improvisatori\",\n    30→        \"Ballet-dancers\",\n    31→        \"Beauty\"\n    32→      ],\n    33→      \"summary\": \"The chapter opens with the devastating spread of the 'Red Death,' a gruesome plague marked by bleeding pores and rapid death, prompting Prince Prospero to isolate himself and a thousand courtiers within a fortified, elaborately designed abbey. Inside, seven uniquely colored rooms—each with stained-glass windows matching their decor—host a lavish masked ball, illuminated only by firelight streaming through the windows from external braziers. The atmosphere is wild and grotesque until a mysterious figure, dressed as the Red Death itself with a blood-smeared mask and shroud, enters and moves silently through the chambers. Prince Prospero, enraged by the blasphemy, pursues the figure with a dagger through all seven rooms, culminating in the black chamber where the figure turns and the prince collapses dead. The revelers rush forward, only to discover the mask and robes are empty, revealing the Red Death itself has infiltrated their sanctuary, and one by one, all die as the ebony clock stops and darkness consumes the abbey.\"\n    34→    }\n    35→  ],\n    36→  \"characters\": [\n    37→    {\n    38→      \"id\": \"char_the_prince_prospero_d85685e9\",\n    39→      \"canonical_name\": \"the Prince Prospero\",\n    40→      \"aliases\": [\n    41→        \"Prospero\"\n    42→      ],\n    43→      \"role\": null,\n    44→      \"appearance\": null,\n    45→      \"personality\": null,\n    46→      \"voice_guidance\": null,\n    47→      \"descriptions\": [],\n    48→      \"relationships\": {},\n    49→      \"evidence\": [],\n    50→      \"voice_notes\": null,\n    51→      \"first_appearance_chapter\": 1,\n    52→      \"mention_count\": 3,\n    53→      \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    54→      \"is_narrator\": false,\n    55→      \"narrative_role\": null\n    56→    },\n    57→    {\n    58→      \"id\": \"1549359c-3187-4144-821d-ce6a2428a0dc\",\n    59→      \"canonical_name\": \"the mummer\",\n    60→      \"aliases\": [],\n    61→      \"role\": null,\n    62→      \"appearance\": {\n    63→        \"summary\": \"The mummer wears a costume dabbled in blood and is fully masked with features resembling the Red Death, including a corpse-like visage and scarlet-stained brow.\",\n    64→        \"age_indication\": \"unknown\",\n    65→        \"distinguishing_features\": [\n    66→          \"Vesture dabbled in blood\",\n    67→          \"Broad brow and features besprinkled with scarlet\",\n    68→          \"Corpse-like mask\",\n    69→          \"Tall figure standing erect and motionless\"\n    70→        ]\n    71→      },\n    72→      \"personality\": {\n    73→        \"summary\": \"The mummer exhibits calculated cruelty and a chilling disregard for human life, using fear as a weapon to dismantle the illusion of safety and control.\",\n    74→        \"traits\": [\n    75→          \"Cruel\",\n    76→          \"Manipulative\",\n    77→          \"Deliberate\",\n    78→          \"Unfazed by fear or confrontation\"\n    79→        ],\n    80→        \"temperament\": \"calm\",\n    81→        \"emotional_range\": \"No emotional expression is evident; the character remains motionless and composed throughout\"\n    82→      },\n    83→      \"voice_guidance\": {\n    84→        \"suggested_tone\": \"unknown\",\n    85→        \"dialect_notes\": \"unknown\",\n    86→        \"verbal_tics\": [],\n    87→        \"formality_level\": \"moderate\",\n    88→        \"example_quotes\": []\n    89→      },\n    90→      \"descriptions\": [\n    91→        {\n    92→          \"text\": \"The mummer is a malevolent figure who infiltrates a masked ball during a plague, impersonating the Red Death in a deliberate act of terror. His actions incite widespread fear, culminate in the death of the prince, and expose the fragility of the revelers' illusion of safety, confirming his role as a destructive antagonist.\",\n    93→          \"source_position\": 1894,\n    94→          \"chapter_index\": null,\n    95→          \"confidence\": \"llm_refined\"\n    96→        }\n    97→      ],\n    98→      \"relationships\": {},\n    99→      \"evidence\": [\n   100→        {\n   101→          \"statement\": \"The mummer assumes the appearance of the Red Death, a symbol of plague and death, to instill terror among the revelers.\",\n   102→          \"quote\": \"the mummer had gone so far as to assume the type of the Red Death. His vesture was dabbled in blood -- and his broad brow, with all the features of the face, was besprinkled with the scarlet...\",\n   103→          \"position\": 10339,\n   104→          \"confidence\": \"high\"\n   105→        },\n   106→        {\n   107→     